src/mako/mako.patch — the desktop's mako (setup.sh: build_mako), against MAKO_TAG/MAKO_COMMIT
(fedokawaii.conf). Three style options, each off until the config sets it:
  shadow-color=#RRGGBBAA #RRGGBBAA   the frame of everything that floats (docs/design-system.md
                                     §4): the border's corner pixels left out, and the shadow —
                                     two rows under the notice (the first from a pixel in to under
                                     the right border, the second a pixel further right) and a
                                     column at its right from its second row down, in the margin
                                     (the surface keeps two rows under the last notice for it)
  summary-icon-color=#RRGGBB[AA]     a summary that opens with one of the desktop's pixel icons
                                     (U+FE000–U+FEFFF): the icon in that ink, its words 8 px on (of
                                     the two spaces after it, one)
  hanging-indent=PX                  the lines after the first under its words (the summary and the
                                     body one paragraph: their line breaks become U+2028), and no
                                     "…" — whole lines, what does not fit cut at a line's end
git apply reads past these lines to the first diff.

